Assessment
0 	<= score <    13:	fail
14 	<= score <=  20: 	pass (for Erasmus students: 19-20 can be equalled to A)

20 pts max pts -> 14 to pass (70%)

11 pts -> “module points” = module tasks, projects, portfolio, attendance, and learning evolution for each module. (This is actually exactly one point per week.)
4 pts -> personal reflections log (there are 16 total, we will round up, so you also get 4 points with 14 reflections) (These are actually 0.25 points per week.)
5 pts -> Final Project. This is the most important part of the class, offering the greatest learning opportunity, and is mandatory to pass (minimum of 2 points as seen above). (Also, the 5 points maximum here reflect one point per week.)
3 extra points -> some extra points for extraordinary performance or help, or small extra projects

Lectures and labs are integrated and, therefore, not strictly separated, so there will be lots of hands-on and interactive activities happening at all times.

